.nh
.TH "PB-UPDATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-update - Update pb from the signed Paperboat release


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb update [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Update pb from the signed Paperboat release

.PP
Download and verify a signed Paperboat release, then review and approve its exact candidate before installation. Check and status are read-only; download never restarts services. Ordinary installation reconnects connections while preserving running shells; process-owner updates warn before ending running work. Recovery uses trusted artifacts.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--approve\fP=""
	install the exact downloaded candidate ID after reviewing it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-check(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-download(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-settings(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-status(1)\fP
